      "description": "A genus of small, nuthatch-like passerines endemic to the Australo-Papuan region, named for their tree-climbing habits that superficially resemble the Northern Hemisphere nuthatches. They move headfirst down tree trunks and along branches, using their strong legs and sharp claws to maintain a firm grip on bark. Their plumage is typically a combination of grey, black, and rufous.",
